4. Restrictions on commercial use

  4.1 You may not engage in Commercial Exploitation of the Software or of
      any Modified Version without the prior written authorization of the
      Licensor. In particular, without such authorization, You may not:

      (a) sell the Software;
      (b) sell a Modified Version;
      (c) offer the Software or a Modified Version as a paid SaaS;
      (d) offer the Software or a Modified Version as a paid hosted or
          managed service;
      (e) charge customers or other Third Parties for access to the Control
          Panel, including its interface or its API;
      (f) commercially redistribute the Software or a Modified Version;
      (g) bundle the Software or a Modified Version into paid products or
          services;
      (h) resell the Software or a Modified Version to customers;
      (i) offer the Software or a Modified Version as part of a commercial
          managed service; or
      (j) commercially distribute hardware that includes the Software or a
          Modified Version, as described in Section 5.

      These restrictions apply even if the Software is described as free,
      included at no additional cost, offered as a bonus, or not separately
      itemized.

  4.2 External access. You may not give customers, external partners or
      any other Third Party access to the Control Panel, whether or not
      You charge for that access, without the prior written authorization
      of the Licensor. This Section does not restrict:

      (a) access to Independent Applications by their users, visitors or
          customers;
      (b) the publication, through the Software, of read-only status pages
          about Your Independent Applications; or
      (c) sharing with Third Parties notifications, reports or exports
          produced by the Software about Your own deployments.

  4.3 You may not remove, circumvent or obscure the restrictions of this
      license, or impose terms on any recipient that conflict with it.


5. Commercial Hardware and Bundled Distribution

  5.1 "Commercial Hardware Distribution" means making the Software or a
      Modified Version available together with hardware that is sold,
      rented, leased or otherwise provided to Third Parties for
      compensation, whether the Software is installed before delivery,
      shipped with the hardware, installed by the seller at or after
      delivery as part of the sale, or provided as a download or image
      intended for that hardware as part of the offering.

  5.2 Without the prior written authorization of the Licensor, You may not:

      (a) pre-install the Software or a Modified Version on hardware
          intended for commercial sale;
      (b) include the Software or a Modified Version in artificial
          intelligence (AI) appliances, or in any other appliances, sold to
          businesses or to any other customer;
      (c) bundle the Software or a Modified Version with servers,
          computers, network-attached storage (NAS) devices or other
          hardware sold commercially;
      (d) sell a hardware product with the Software or a Modified Version
          included, even if the Software has no separately itemized price;
      (e) use the Software or a Modified Version as a free bonus,
          additional feature or incentive to facilitate the sale of
          commercial hardware; or
      (f) rent or lease hardware with the Software or a Modified Version
          included as part of a commercial offering.

      This Section applies whether the Software is the main selling point
      of the product or merely one of its components, such as its
      administration panel alongside an operating system and other
      software.

  5.3 Exceptions. This Section does not prohibit:

      (a) a person or company that has purchased, rented or otherwise
          acquired hardware from independently obtaining the Software,
          from the Licensor's official distribution channels or from a free
          redistribution permitted by Section 6, and installing it on that
          hardware, on its own initiative, for its own permitted use;
      (b) a company installing and using the Software for Internal Use on
          servers, computers or other hardware that it owns or controls,
          including hardware it has purchased, rented or leased; or
      (c) a company using the Software for Internal Use to manage hardware
          or devices that it sells, provided that the Software itself is
          not distributed with that hardware and that its customers are not
          given access to the Control Panel.


